#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# longest_common_sequence

#% text
# `longest_common_sequence(a, b)` gives a longest list of elements (characters of strings) that occur in both `a` and `b` in the same order, not necessarily next to each other.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For strings the result is a string; for lists a list.

#% item
# `longest_common_subsequence` requires the elements to be consecutive.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
longest_common_sequence("abcdef", "xbdy")
#% output
#= "bd"

#% cell
longest_common_sequence([1, 3, 2, 5, 4], [3, 5, 2, 4])
#% output
#= [3, 2, 4]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `longest_common_subsequence`
